From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilies CHERGUI <ichergui@nvidia.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] utils: Serialize UUID generation

GenerateUUID() shares one static boost::uuids::random_generator
between all callers without a lock. Since Boost 1.86 the generator is
a ChaCha20/12 PRNG that hands out words from an internal block buffer,
and Boost documents its classes as only as thread-safe as an int.

Triton loads models on several threads (four by default). When two
Python models are loaded at the same time, their stub launchers can
read the same words and get the same UUID, and then the same shared
memory region name. One launcher then fails to create the region with
"File exists" and removes it in its error path. The other launcher's
stub then fails to open the region with "No such file or directory",
so both models fail to load.

Guard the generator with a mutex.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Ilies CHERGUI <ichergui@nvidia.com>
---
 src/pb_utils.cc | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/pb_utils.cc b/src/pb_utils.cc
index 79b45ec..6f6bd83 100644
--- a/src/pb_utils.cc
+++ b/src/pb_utils.cc
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@
 #include <sys/stat.h>
 
 #include <fstream>
+#include <mutex>
 
 #ifdef _WIN32
 #include <windows.h>
@@ -351,8 +352,15 @@ IsExecutableFile(const std::string& filepath)
 std::string
 GenerateUUID()
 {
+  // The generator keeps internal state and is not thread-safe, and models
+  // are loaded concurrently.
+  static std::mutex generator_mutex;
   static boost::uuids::random_generator generator;
-  boost::uuids::uuid uuid = generator();
+  boost::uuids::uuid uuid;
+  {
+    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(generator_mutex);
+    uuid = generator();
+  }
   return boost::uuids::to_string(uuid);
 }
 
